    "title": "Fan Interruption and Knicks' Playoff Win Over Spurs",
    "text": "• The New York Knicks played the San Antonio Spurs on Wednesday night.\n• A fan ran onto the court in the fourth quarter, appearing to attempt a selfie with Victor Wembanyama.\n• The fan was removed by security and play resumed after a brief stoppage.\n• Knicks guard Jalen Brunson experienced two separate incidents involving his knee and ankle during the game.\n• Brunson returned to the game after both incidents and finished with 30 points.\n• The Knicks defeated the Spurs 105-95.\n• This marked the Knicks' 12th consecutive playoff victory.",
    "summary": "The New York Knicks began their pursuit of their first title since 1973 on Wednesday night in a matchup against Victor Wembanyama and the San Antonio Spurs. But amid the tension of a tightly contested fourth quarter, an overexcited fan briefly stole the spotlight in pursuit of what he hoped would be a once-in-a-lifetime photo. The fan came from the sideline opposite the team benches, starting from behind the play and running into San Antonio’s offensive end.",
